# More outputs with a shift register
# Level 3 - Sensors and motors
#
# Drive eight LEDs from three pins with a 74HC595 chip.
# You learn: the shift library, binary numbers (0b...) and the << operator.
# You need: a 74HC595: data (DS) to pin 11, clock (SH_CP) to pin 12, latch (ST_CP) to pin 8,
# eight LEDs with resistors on its outputs Q0-Q7, VCC and MR to 5V, GND and OE to GND.

board uno
use mujard.shift

leds = shift.out_register(data: pin 11, clock: pin 12, latch: pin 8)

var pattern = 0b0000_0001          # one bit for each LED; _ is just for reading

every 100 ms:
    leds.write(pattern)
    pattern = pattern << 1         # move the light one place along
    if pattern > 0b1000_0000:
        pattern = 0b0000_0001
